Dataset rlp_ascode_check {
  label: 'RLP as-code check (dataset-level dimension)'
  description: '''
    RLP as-code with a CROSS-MODEL dimension defined at DATASET level.

    has_access is true when dim_b.role OR dim_c.role matches the current user's h_role.

    Note on syntax: the permission must reference the dataset-level field with ref('fact_a', 'has_access').
    The r(fact_a.has_access) form does NOT resolve dataset-level fields and fails to compile with
    "Cannot find field 'has_access' in model 'fact_a'".

    HOW TO CHECK (RLP as-code is not enforced in the dev workspace, and admins bypass RLP - so this must be
    published to production and checked while impersonating a non-admin):

    1. Publish this dataset to production.
    2. Top-right menu -> View and Edit as -> pick an Explorer / Viewer user.
    3. Set that user's h_role attribute, then explore fact_a and check which rows come back.

    fact_a data and expected rows:

      id | dim_b.role | dim_c.role | has_access(admin) | has_access(analyst)
      ---+------------+------------+-------------------+--------------------
       1 | admin      | admin      | true              | false
       2 | admin      | analyst    | true              | true
       3 | analyst    | admin      | true              | true
       4 | analyst    | analyst    | false             | true

    So: h_role = admin   -> rows 1, 2, 3
        h_role = analyst -> rows 2, 3, 4

    has_access is left visible (not hidden) on purpose so it can be put on screen next to dim_b.role and
    dim_c.role while checking.
  '''
  data_source_name: 'demodb'

  models: [
    fact_a,
    dim_b,
    dim_c,
  ]

  relationships: [
    relationship(fact_a.b_id > dim_b.id, true),
    relationship(fact_a.c_id > dim_c.id, true),
  ]

  dimension has_access {
    model: fact_a
    label: 'Has Access'
    type: 'truefalse'
    definition: @aql or(
      dim_b.role == H.current_user.h_role,
      dim_c.role == H.current_user.h_role
    ) ;;
  }

  permission fact_a_access {
    field: ref('fact_a', 'has_access')
    operator: 'is'
    value: true
  }

  view {
    model fact_a {}
    model dim_b {}
    model dim_c {}
  }
}
